{
  "requirement": "`OutlineLang` defines the language interface. Each implementation supplies its\nname, claimed extensions, and outlining operation. Cloning a language shares\nits prepared configuration instead of rebuilding it or copying it in proportion\nto its size. Its result uses the public items, spans, and hashes under\n{cite}`requirements.sdk.outlines.items`. Filename extensions omit the leading dot.\n\n```rust,ignore\npub trait OutlineLang:\n    Clone\n    + Send\n    + Sync {\n    fn name(&self) -> &str;\n    fn extensions(&self) -> &[&str];\n    fn outline(&self, source: &str) -> Result<Outline, OutlineError>;\n    fn fingerprint_scheme(&self) -> &str;\n\n    fn search_structure(\n        &self,\n        _source: &str,\n        _rule: &Map<String, Value>,\n    ) -> Result<Vec<Span>, OutlineError> { ... }\n}\n```",
  "determination": true,
  "rationale": "structural: Structural obligations in `requirements.sdk.outlines.language_provider`:\n- The trait `OutlineLang: Clone + Send + Sync`. An alternative without those supertraits would violate the prescribed declaration. `crates/trust-but-verify/src/outline/contents.rs#trait[OutlineLang]` declares exactly these supertraits.\n- The prescribed method signatures. A language could expose the same results through different signatures, such as `name(&self) -> String` or an `outline` that returns a different type. The trait declares `name`, `extensions`, `outline` and `fingerprint_scheme` with the stated signatures, in `trait[OutlineLang]/fn[name]`, `fn[extensions]`, `fn[outline]` and `fn[fingerprint_scheme]`. It also declares a default `search_structure` that takes `&serde_json::Map<String, serde_json::Value>` and returns `Result<Vec<Span>, OutlineError>`. `outline` returns `Result<Outline, OutlineError>`, so results use the public `Outline` type from the items requirement.\n- Cloning shares prepared configuration instead of rebuilding or copying it. An implementation that deep-copied or rebuilt its rules on `Clone` would violate this. The trait doc states the contract. The bundled implementations, generated by `crates/trust-but-verify/src/outline/languages/mod.rs#macro[language]`, are zero-sized `Clone, Copy` structs. They read a shared `$profile` path, so cloning cannot rebuild or copy configuration in proportion to its size. The macro also supplies `name`, `extensions`, `outline` (through `parse_with` and `Outline::from_legacy`), `fingerprint_scheme` and `search_structure`, all taken from the profile.\n\nThe other clauses are observable behavior, or are covered by their own sub-requirements. These are the clause that extensions omit the leading dot, and the `fingerprint_scheme` and `structural_search` children, which are marked on their trait methods. The two roots therefore cover the structural obligations. The trait is also implemented by the test-only `CustomLanguage` and similar types in `tests/outline_content.rs`, which are not roots here.\n\nbehavioral: The marked tests cover each behavioral obligation in `requirements.sdk.outlines.language_provider`.\n\n- **Name, extensions and outlining operation.**\n  - `crates/trust-but-verify/tests/outline_content.rs#fn[bundled_languages_claim_extensions_and_supply_the_same_public_outline]` has a helper `check`. It asserts `name()` is non-empty, `extensions()` equals the exact expected lists, and `fingerprint_scheme()` matches. It calls `outline()` directly.\n  - Every expected extension list is written without a leading dot, for example `[\"rs\"]` and `[\"md\", \"markdown\"]`. The exact comparison enforces the no-dot rule.\n  - The test checks `PlainText` has name `plain-text` and no extensions.\n  - `crates/trust-but-verify/tests/outline_content.rs#fn[explicit_languages_share_configuration_and_retain_their_scheme]` checks a custom implementation's `name()`, `extensions()` and `outline()` result.\n- **Cloning shares prepared configuration.** The custom-language test clones `CustomLanguage` and asserts `Arc::ptr_eq` on the configuration. It also drops the originals and the scheme `Arc`, then confirms the scheme survives. The bundled languages are zero-sized, which `check` asserts with `size_of::<L>() == 0`, so cloning them neither rebuilds nor copies anything.\n- **Result uses the public items, spans and hashes.**\n  - `check` verifies the raw `outline()` root has an empty selector and span `0..len`.\n  - It verifies the raw selectors match those of `OutlineContent`'s outline.\n  - It verifies every item span is a valid slice of the source.\n  - The custom-language test asserts the root span, the structural hash and the item's own hash.\n- **`search_structure`.** `check` calls `search_structure` on each bundled language and asserts the ranges are non-empty and valid. `crates/trust-but-verify/src/outline/tests.rs#fn[custom_provider_handles_generated_content_and_structural_search]` covers a custom provider. `crates/trust-but-verify/src/sources/tests.rs#fn[registered_grammars_match_their_profiles_and_parse_the_selected_language]` checks the registered grammars.\n- **Trait shape.** `crates/trust-but-verify/tests/public_api.rs#fn[public_exports_match_the_appendix]` checks the public API inventory. The trait signature is a structural obligation, so it needs no behavioral test.\n\nI found no gap.",
  "references": "df05caa874a771acf430e14d443df1d8581090f8b83152178cfb66d9b16d2cc5",
